3,134 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 66 people. Revenue per employee of $2.9M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, improving at 8%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $52K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Netlist, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $2.0B market cap on $189M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +37% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at -201% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 13% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $15M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -20.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -546.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.8% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 20% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 222% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.2166239496479903},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 51/100): roic below cost of capital; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Technology peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Does Ultra Low Latency DDR5 Launch Change The Bull Case For Netlist (NLST)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/tech/otc-nlst/netlist/news/does-ultra-low-latency-ddr5-launch-change-the-bull-case-for","date":"2026-10-29","timestamp":1793284176.595,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.077,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["product"]},{"title":"Netlist (OTCMKTS:NLST) Stock Price Up 7.9% \u2013 What\u2019s Next?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/26/netlist-otcmktsnlst-stock-price-up-7-9-whats-next.html","date":"2026-10-26","timestamp":1793044853.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.84,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Netlist (NLST) Is Back In The Spotlight","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/tech/otc-nlst/net